() Tj T*
(- Detection combines behavior rules, threat intelligence matches, statistical baselines) Tj T*
(    and two models. None of them proves an attack happened, and none proves that one did) Tj T*
(    not.) Tj T*
(- The saved network model runs only on flow data with its 78 CIC-IDS2017 features. It) Tj T*
(    has not been validated here, no preprocessing pipeline was saved with it, and its) Tj T*
(    output is uncalibrated, so no accuracy or prediction confidence is claimed.) Tj T*
(- The anomaly model was trained on synthetic normal activity, and does not run on live) Tj T*
(    telemetry. Its findings are statistical anomalies, not confirmed attacks.) Tj T*
(- Threat intelligence only covers known indicators, and the bundled feed is synthetic.) Tj T*
(    No match does not mean an event is safe.) Tj T*
(- Performance metrics compare results with labels on synthetic or supplied data. They do) Tj T*
(    not predict performance on real attacks.) Tj T*
(- The synthetic scenarios and the detection rules were written by the same team, so) Tj T*
(    scenario results show the pipeline works as designed.) Tj T*
(- Behavioral checks need history. An entity with too little history is not judged.) Tj T*
(- Window-based rules cite every matching event in their window, so a normal event inside) Tj T*
(    an attack window counts as an event-level false positive.) Tj T*
(- Risk is an investigation priority, not the probability that an attack is real.) Tj T*
(- Historical analysis is read-only. Every response action is a recommendation that needs) Tj T*
(    an analyst, and runs only in simulation. No firewall, account, host or process is) Tj T*
(    changed.) Tj T*
(- Analyst names are self-reported: there are no user accounts.) Tj T*
